  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "💀 Warhammer 40k Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Space Marines by Chapter, Imperial Guard with their regiment, and Aeldari of the craftworlds."
    },
    "intro": "In the grim darkness of the far future, a name tells you who someone serves. An Ultramarine sounds like a <a href=\"roman-name-generator.html\">Roman</a> legionary (Marneus Calgar, Cato Sicarius), a Space Wolf like a saga hero (Logan Grimnar, Ragnar Blackmane), and an Imperial Guard officer comes with a regiment attached. This **Warhammer 40k name generator** builds names for Space Marines in three Chapter styles, the Imperial Guard and the Aeldari.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Space Marine names by Chapter",
        "content": "<p>Each Space Marine Chapter recruits from its own worlds and keeps its own culture, and names follow:</p><ul><li><strong>Ultramarines</strong> and similar Chapters have Roman-sounding names: Marneus Calgar, Cato Sicarius, Uriel Ventris. A first name and a surname, often with a rank in front.</li><li><strong>Space Wolves</strong> come from Fenris and have Norse names and <a href=\"epithet-generator.html\">epithets</a>: Logan Grimnar, Ragnar Blackmane, Bjorn the Fell-Handed.</li><li><strong>Blood Angels</strong> and <strong>Dark Angels</strong> lean towards angelic and Renaissance Italian names, often used alone: Dante and Mephiston of the Blood Angels, Azrael of the Dark Angels.</li></ul><p>Ranks come first: Brother for a battle-brother, then Sergeant, Lieutenant, Captain, or a specialist role like Chaplain, Librarian, Apothecary or Techmarine.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Imperial Guard names",
        "content": "<p>The Imperial Guard, or Astra Militarum, is made of regiments raised from a single world and named after it with a number: the Cadian 8th, the Tanith First and Only from the Gaunt's Ghosts novels. A Guard name is ordinary, a little rough, and nearly always comes with a rank and a regiment.</p><p>Famous examples include Lord Castellan Ursarkar E. Creed of Cadia, Commissar Sebastian Yarrick of Armageddon, and Commissar Ciaphas Cain. The generator's regiments come from well-known Guard worlds (Cadian, Catachan, Valhallan, Vostroyan, Mordian, Tallarn, Elysian, Krieg, Armageddon and more) with a random number, so you get a regiment that sounds right without copying a famous one.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Aeldari names",
        "content": "<p>The Aeldari, called Eldar in older editions, live on vast craftworld ships such as Ulthwé, Biel-Tan, Iyanden, Saim-Hann and Alaitoc. Their names are long, flowing and elegant: Eldrad Ulthran, the great Farseer of Ulthwé; Prince Yriel of Iyanden; Illic Nightspear of Alaitoc.</p><p>Aeldari follow the Path, devoting themselves to one role at a time, so the <em>With rank and unit</em> format names a role (Farseer, Warlock, Autarch, Exarch, Ranger, Spiritseer) and a craftworld.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Picking a name for your army",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Name your characters, not every model.</strong> A named Captain and Sergeant give an army personality; the rest can be Brother this and Trooper that.</li><li><strong>Make a successor Chapter.</strong> If your Chapter is your own, pick the style of its founding Chapter, then add your own twist.</li><li><strong>Number your regiment with care.</strong> A Guard regiment with a high number suggests a world that has sent many, and lost many.</li></ul><p>For other 40k factions, try the <a href=\"warhammer-orc-name-generator.html\">Warhammer Orc</a> and <a href=\"ogryn-name-generator.html\">Ogryn</a> name generators. Looking for names for a war hammer, the weapon? See the <a href=\"hammer-name-generator.html\">Hammer Name Generator</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do Space Marine names work?",
        "answer": "A rank, then a name in the style of the Chapter's homeworld: Roman-sounding for the Ultramarines (Marneus Calgar), Norse for the Space Wolves (Ragnar Blackmane), angelic or Italian for the Blood Angels (Dante, Mephiston)."
      },
      {
        "question": "How are Imperial Guard regiments named?",
        "answer": "After the world they were raised on and a number: the Cadian 8th, the Catachan 2nd. The Tanith First and Only from Gaunt's Ghosts is a famous exception."
      },
      {
        "question": "What's the difference between Eldar and Aeldari?",
        "answer": "The same people. Games Workshop renamed the Eldar as the Aeldari in the eighth edition of Warhammer 40,000."
      },
      {
        "question": "I was looking for war hammer weapon names.",
        "answer": "They're on the <a href=\"hammer-name-generator.html\">Hammer Name Generator</a>, which used to live at this address."
      }
    ]
